# Part 5, row 7: `x.f(y)` becomes `f(x, y)`. The receiver is argument zero, and
# the resolver already decided which `f` — the IR records the linkage, so a
# Heroes function and a built-in of the same shape cannot be confused later.
function double(n: i64) -> i64
    return n * 2

function main()
    print([1, 2].len().double())
